{{also|Appendix:Variations of "eg"}}
==Hungarian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{audio|Hu-ég.ogg|Audio|lang=hu}}
* {{hyphenation|ég|lang=hu}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{inh|hu|fiu-pro|*säŋe||air}}. Possible cognates are limited to Baltic-Finnic (e.g. {{cog|fi|sää||weather}}) and {{cog|koi|сынӧд||warm air}}.<ref>{{R:Uralonet|879}}</ref><ref>{{R:Zaicz 2006}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{hu-noun|pl=egek}}

# [[sky]] {{gloss|the part of the atmosphere which can be seen above a specific place}}
#*{{quote-journal
|lang=hu
|year=1937
|author=László Balás-Piri
|title=A múzeum képtára
|periodical=Székesfehérvári Szemle
|url=http://epa.oszk.hu/01900/01940/00023/pdf/szfvsz_07_03-04_1937_048-061.pdf
|passage=A halvány kék '''égen''' fehér felhők vonulnak.
|translation=White clouds are marching across the pale blue '''sky'''.}}
# {{lb|hu|also in the plural}} [[heaven]] {{gloss|the abode of God and of the blessed dead}}
#*{{quote-book
|lang=hu
|year=1908
|author={{w|Grazia Deledda}}
|author2=Mrs. Károly Sebestyén (translator)
|chapter=4
|title=A repkény
|url=http://mek.oszk.hu/12200/12229/12229.htm
|passage=Ha van Isten az '''égben''', úgy meg fog nekünk bocsátani.
|translation=If there is a God in '''heaven''', He will forgive us.}}
# {{lb|hu|by extension|in set phrases}} [[heaven]] as a [[euphemism]] for [[God]] {{gloss|the supreme being and principal object of faith in Christianity}}
#*{{quote-book
|lang=hu
|year=1899
|author=Lenke Bajza Beniczky
|chapter=8
|title=Sára története
|url=http://mek.oszk.hu/19000/19001/19001.pdf
|passage=Hála az '''égnek''', hogy megszabadulunk tőlük.
|translation=Thank '''heavens''' we'll be rid of them.}}

